\p{The material in this section is presented via a [POGIL activity](https://hendrix-cs.github.io/csci382/pub/divide-and-conquer-intro.pdf).}

\p{A classic example of a divide-and-conquer algorithm is \em{mergesort}, which works by splitting the input list into two halves, recursively sorting each half, and then merging the sorted halves together.}

